// Source: Spotify's own filings on SEC EDGAR, CIK 0001639920 — the interim 6-K for each of Q1, Q2 and Q3 and the 20-F for each
// year (Q4 is the year less the nine months), 1Q21–2Q26. Reported figures, which rule 10 allows in a file. Generated by
// scratchpad hm/spot_hm.py reading the statements; not typed. All amounts are EUR (Spotify reports in euros).
//   EBITDA     operating income + depreciation and amortization + share-based compensation, per quarter (Q2 and Q3 from
//              the year-to-date cash-flow lines, Q4 = year less nine months). This ties to the Results dataset to the euro
//              from 2Q25 on; for 1Q24, 3Q24 and 4Q24 the Bloomberg figure in Results is EUR 82–96M higher (it also adds back
//              social costs, which the filings do not isolate), so the module uses Results for 1Q24 onward and this file before.
//   EPS (LTM)  diluted EPS, built only from reported figures: the last fiscal year, less the same year-to-date a year earlier,
//              plus the year-to-date now (EPS does not add across quarters because the share count moves).
//   shares     weighted-average diluted ordinary shares for the quarter, millions; Q4 = the full-year weighted average.
//   cash       cash and cash equivalents, period end.   sti  short term investments, period end.
//   notes      Exchangeable Notes (the only borrowing; none after 1Q25, one current balance at Dec 2025 settled in 2026).
//   net debt   notes - cash - short term investments (negative = net cash). Lease liabilities and long term investments
//              (equity stakes) are left out, as in the TSMC and Meta files.
// The "filed" date is when the statements became public; the chart steps each series on that date.
// [quarter, balance-sheet date, filed, EBITDA (EUR M), diluted EPS LTM (EUR), diluted shares (M), cash, short term investments, Exchangeable Notes, net debt]
